-- title:
--   Horizon-$T$ SAP purchase process, regret $\Delta_\pi(T,v)$ and mean squared error $\delta_t$
-- statement:
--   Fix $w$, $v$ and SAP$(\alpha,\beta)$ with initial value $\varrho_1$, and a horizon $T\in\mathbb N$.
--
--   1. A **horizon-$T$ SAP process** is a probability space $(\Omega,\mathbb P)$ with measurable (no-)purchases $X_1,\dots,X_T$ such that, for each $t\le T$, conditionally on the history $X_1,\dots,X_{t-1}$ the purchase $X_t$ has the choice law of the offered assortment $S_t=[w^{-1}(\varrho_t),1]$. Equivalently, for every event $E$ of the history and every measurable set $A$ of purchases,
--   $$\mathbb P(E\cap\{X_t\in A\})=\int_E \mathbb P\big(X^{[w^{-1}(\varrho_t(\omega)),1]}\in A\big)\,d\mathbb P(\omega).$$
--   2. The **regret** of the policy is
--   $$\Delta_\pi(T,v)=\sum_{t=1}^T\mathbb E_\pi\Big[\max_{S\in\mathcal S}r(S,v)-r(S_t,v)\Big].$$
--   3. The **mean squared error** of the iterate is $\delta_t=\mathbb E_\pi[(\varrho_t-\varrho^*)^2]$.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The paper says the purchase is distributed as $X^{S}$ "conditionally on $S_t=S$"; this is read as conditioning on the whole history, which is what the policy-dependent expectation $\mathbb E_\pi$ of (3) requires. Indices are 0-based ($n=t-1$), the purchases are a sequence $X_n$ of which those with $n\ge T$ are unconstrained, and the history events are the sets measurable for the σ-algebra generated by $X_0,\dots,X_{n-1}$.
-- source:
--   Peeters, den Boer, Mandjes, Continuous Assortment Optimization with Logit Choice Probabilities under Incomplete Information, arXiv:1807.06497v4, §3, (2)–(3), pp.7–8; §4.2, p.11; App. A.1, p.36 (δ_t)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ContAssortLogit_Model
import Definitions.Def_ContAssortLogit_Policy
open MeasureTheory Set

namespace ContAssortLogit

universe u

/-- A horizon-`T` purchase process generated by SAP(α, β) under preference function `v`
(arXiv:1807.06497v4, §3, (2), pp.7–8, and §4.2, p.11): a probability measure `P` on `Ω` and
measurable (no-)purchases `X 0, …, X (T − 1)` such that, for each `n < T`, conditionally on the
history `X 0, …, X (n − 1)` the purchase `X n` has the choice law (1) of the assortment
`S = [w⁻¹(ϱ_n), 1]` offered by SAP. Written as the joint law of history and purchase: for every
history event `E` and every measurable `A`,
`P(E ∩ {X n ∈ A}) = ∫_E choiceLaw v [w⁻¹(ϱ_n(ω)), 1] (A) dP(ω)`.

**Formalization Note.** The paper's "conditionally on `S_t = S`, the purchase `X_t` is distributed
as `X^S`" is read as conditioning on the whole history `(S_1, X_1, …, S_{t−1}, X_{t−1})`, as the
expectation `E_π` of (3) requires; for SAP the assortments are functions of the past purchases.
Index `n` is the paper's period `n + 1`. Coordinates `X n` with `n ≥ T` are unconstrained. -/
def IsSAPProcess (w v : ℝ → ℝ) (α β ϱ₁ : ℝ) (T : ℕ) {Ω : Type u} [MeasurableSpace Ω]
    (P : Measure Ω) (X : ℕ → Ω → PurchaseSpace) : Prop :=
  IsProbabilityMeasure P ∧ (∀ n < T, Measurable (X n)) ∧
    ∀ n < T, ∀ E : Set Ω,
      MeasurableSet[MeasurableSpace.comap (fun ω (i : Fin n) => X i ω) inferInstance] E →
      ∀ A : Set PurchaseSpace, MeasurableSet A →
        P (E ∩ X n ⁻¹' A) =
          ∫⁻ ω in E, choiceLaw v (sapAssort w (sapRho w α β ϱ₁ (fun i => X i ω) n)) A ∂P

/-- The regret of SAP(α, β) over horizon `T` (arXiv:1807.06497v4, §3, eq. (3), p.8):
`Δ_π(T, v) = Σ_{t=1}^T E_π[max_{S ∈ 𝒮} r(S, v) − r(S_t, v)]`, with `S_t = [w⁻¹(ϱ_t), 1]`.

**Formalization Note.** The sum runs over the 0-based indices `n = 0, …, T − 1`; the maximum is
`optRev w v`. -/
noncomputable def regret (w v : ℝ → ℝ) (α β ϱ₁ : ℝ) (T : ℕ) {Ω : Type u} [MeasurableSpace Ω]
    (P : Measure Ω) (X : ℕ → Ω → PurchaseSpace) : ℝ :=
  ∑ n ∈ Finset.range T,
    ∫ ω, (optRev w v - rev w v (sapAssort w (sapRho w α β ϱ₁ (fun i => X i ω) n))) ∂P

/-- The mean squared error `δ_t = E_π[(ϱ_t − ϱ*)²]` of the SAP iterate (arXiv:1807.06497v4,
App. A.1, p.36), at 0-based index `n` (the paper's `δ_{n+1}`). -/
noncomputable def sapMSE (w v : ℝ → ℝ) (α β ϱ₁ : ℝ) {Ω : Type u} [MeasurableSpace Ω]
    (P : Measure Ω) (X : ℕ → Ω → PurchaseSpace) (n : ℕ) : ℝ :=
  ∫ ω, (sapRho w α β ϱ₁ (fun i => X i ω) n - optRev w v) ^ 2 ∂P

end ContAssortLogit


